// Fluent build blocks — the library half of `@BuildBlock(P)` (fluent spec §6–§9).
//
// The compiler owns the block: which trailing blocks are build blocks, which
// statements are reached expressions, and the `@SourceSite` each one carries.
// Everything else — storage, ordering, erasure, identity, diagnostics — belongs
// to the sink written here, in ordinary sx.
//
// A build-accepting function declares its block parameter last:
//
//     column :: (gap: f32, content: @BuildBlock(Drawable)) { ... }
//
// and replays it into a sink:
//
//     content.run(*sink);
//
// Each standalone expression in the block whose type conforms to the protocol
// becomes one `sink.expression(initializer)` call. The initializer is an
// `@Init(V)` over the CONCRETE `V`, so the sink reserves `size_of(V)` and writes
// the expression straight into its own storage; nothing is materialized, copied,
// or erased before the sink asks for it. Provenance rides on the initializer:
// `value.site()`.

// What a sink promises (spec §6.1). A compiler-maintained contract, and an
// ordinary constraint protocol: no vtable, no erasure — `expression`
// monomorphizes for each concrete `V` the block reaches, which is what lets the
// sink see `V`'s size, alignment, and methods.
//
// There is no site parameter: the initializer is the single source of expression
// provenance, so a sink that wants it asks `value.site()` and cannot be handed a
// site belonging to some other expression.
//
// A sink that returns without writing leaves the source expression unevaluated.
// One that must materialize everything simply writes unconditionally.
@BuildSink :: protocol(P: Type) constraint {
    expression :: (self: *Self, value: @Init($V/P));
}

// Side-effect-free facts about a build block (spec §7). A compiler-maintained
// contract: the compiler synthesizes these values, so the field set is a
// compiler + stdlib contract. Produced only when `content.shape()` is called —
// capturing-only programs do not pay for it. Counts and sizes are
// protocol-independent; association with a block protocol is by use site, not by
// a monomorphic type argument (constraint protocols are not runtime type args).
@BuildShape :: struct {
    static_expressions: i32 = 0;
    dynamic_regions: i32 = 0;
    known_bytes: ?i64 = null;
    max_alignment: i64 = 1;
}



